      "synthesis": {
        "main_text_has_explicit_synthesis": true,
        "si_used": false,
        "procedure": "PrCl3 (0.5 mmol = 91 mg) and 1,3-thiazole (C3H3NS, 2.5 mmol = 210 mg) were sealed in an evacuated Duran glass ampoule. The reaction starts immediately upon contact of the reagents at room temperature. Highly reflecting transparent light-green crystals form on the ampoule walls; formation and crystallization occur within less than 5 min. The tetramer co-crystallizes with equal amounts of [Pr2Cl6(thz)8] and ten lattice thiazole molecules. Water/OH ligands are attributed to residual water in thiazole (purity 99%); reactions with pre-dried thiazole or deliberate added water give other unresolved products.",
